s of biological stores."}, {"id": "B", "text": "It compares carbon sequestration with nitrogen fixation."}, {"id": "C", "text": "It explains how to build a direct air capture plant."}, {"id": "D", "text": "It argues that climate change cannot be limited."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Carbon sequestration", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_sequestration', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M23-TS010', 'A', ARRAY['A']::TEXT[], 'The passage moves from definition to types and then to durability concerns.', '{"C": "No plant design is described.", "B": "Nitrogen fixation is not mentioned.", "D": "The text says sequestration plays a role in limiting climate change."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M23-CE010', 'HDSAT-RW-M23-CE010', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence (Textual)', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Carbon sequestration is a natural process of storing carbon in a carbon pool. It plays a crucial role in effectively managing the global carbon cycle and limiting climate change by reducing the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere. There are two main types of carbon sequestration: biologic (also called biosequestration) and geologic. Biologic carbon sequestration is a naturally occurring process as part of the carbon cycle. Humans can enhance it through deliberate actions and use of technology. Carbon dioxide (CO2) is naturally captured from the atmosphere through biological, chemical, and physical processes. These processes can be accelerated for example through changes in land use and agricultural practices, called carbon farming. Artificial processes have also been devised to produce similar effects. This approach is called carbon capture and storage. It involves using technology to capture and sequester (store) CO2 that is produced from human activities underground or under the sea bed. Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air as they grow, and bind it into biomass. However, biological stores (such as forests and kelp beds) may be temporary carbon sinks, as long-term sequestration cannot be guaranteed. Wildfires, disease, economic pressures, and changing political priorities may release the sequestered carbon back into the atmosphere.', 'Which quotation from the text most directly supports the claim that biological carbon storage may be temporary?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Carbon sequestration is a natural process of storing carbon in a carbon pool."}, {"id": "B", "text": "There are two main types of carbon sequestration: biologic and geologic."}, {"id": "C", "text": "However, biological stores (such as forests and kelp beds) may be temporary carbon sinks, as long-term sequestration cannot be guaranteed."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air as they grow, and bind it into biomass."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Carbon sequestration", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_sequestration', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M23-CE010', 'C', ARRAY['C']::TEXT[], 'The correct quotation explicitly calls biological stores potentially temporary.', '{"A": "This sentence defines sequestration.", "B": "This sentence names the two types.", "D": "This sentence describes how plants take up carbon."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
